[sai-00194] helpful=0 harmful=0 :: When a prompt requests a .docx file, you must use the Python 'python-docx' library to generate a real binary file. Do not provide a text-based simulation. Ensure the Python script explicitly populates all rubric-mandated fields (e.g., cap rates, deposit amounts, notification clauses) into the document structure.
[sai-00195] helpful=0 harmful=0 :: When a prompt provides a reference dataset (e.g., .xlsx) and requests binary file outputs (e.g., PDF flyers, reports), treat the reference file as the mandatory source of truth. Use Python to load, filter, and process this data. Do not hallucinate details or simulate the file structure with text tables. Use libraries like 'fpdf' or 'reportlab' to generate the actual binary files, ensuring all rubric-mandated assets (logos, photos, specific data columns) are programmatically embedded. Perform a 'Rubric-to-Structure' mapping before coding to ensure every granular requirement is met in the final binary output.
