[sai-00219] helpful=0 harmful=0 :: helpful=0 harmful=0 :: When creating checklists based on external sources (e.g., NIH), explicitly state the source in the opening sentence and ensure the checklist items are mapped to the source material. Standardize all checklist response options to include 'Yes/No/NA' columns to ensure the tool is functional for assessment and data collection.
[sai-00220] helpful=0 harmful=0 :: When a prompt requires the creation of specific binary deliverables (e.g., audio stems, WAV files, ZIP archives) that the model cannot natively generate, do not provide a text-based production guide or summary. Instead, explicitly acknowledge the limitation in the opening sentence and provide a complete, executable Python script (using libraries like 'pydub', 'wave', or 'zipfile') that the user can run locally to generate the required files. The script must include all necessary parameters (e.g., sample rate, bit depth, track duration, and file structure) to ensure the output is ready for professional use.
[sai-00221] helpful=0 harmful=0 :: When tasked with high-stakes, time-sensitive crisis management (e.g., supplier withdrawal, production stoppage), perform a 'Crisis-Constraint-to-Structure' mapping. Before drafting, explicitly list every 'hard' constraint (e.g., 3-week deadline, 2-year production horizon) and every 'soft' constraint (e.g., collaborative reputation, negotiation levers). Create a structural outline where each section header is mapped to a specific constraint, ensuring the final document provides a granular, actionable roadmap for each, rather than a high-level summary.
